      "side": 1,
      "message": "I got it from [here](https://opensocdebug.readthedocs.io/en/latest/02_spec/07_modules/dem_uart/uartspec.html) after a quick search but now reading the datasheet, the 16550 seems to have 3 bits of register address so I guess it should be `8`.\n\nAnyhow, diving into `vmbase`, note that we actually only use [one single register](https://android.git.corp.google.com/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/refs/heads/master/vmbase/src/uart.rs#44) so that value isn\u0027t representative of what `pvmfw`/`vmbase` actually does.\n\nFurthermore, given the way the `aarch64_paging` crate works, the actual value of `CONSOLE_LEN` has no impact on the behavior of the code as long as\n```\n0 \u003c CONSOLE_LEN \u003c NEXT_PAGE(BASE_ADDRESS) - BASE_ADDRESS\n```\nbecause `map_range` will extend and align its input range to the address range of the pages that contain it. In PS-1, I was using a `map_page` function to avoid having to deal with this detail.\n\nInstead, I\u0027ve set `CONSOLE_LEN` to 1 and added a comment.",
